1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,516
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:02,966 --> 00:00:05,674
and it puts the whole class together.

3
00:00:06,574 --> 00:00:09,662
You have a boss, with ships and objectives and a hook.

4
00:00:10,112 --> 00:00:13,686
And you know how to write a scene, a call, and an answer.

5
00:00:15,486 --> 00:00:17,625
Today, at last, she speaks.

6
00:00:18,525 --> 00:00:21,611
And all of her voice goes in the one file you already have.

7
00:00:22,811 --> 00:00:25,945
Last time, the crew had ten minutes to sink the Morrigan,

8
00:00:26,395 --> 00:00:28,992
and nothing warned them as the time ran down.

9
00:00:29,892 --> 00:00:31,938
Here's the warning we're about to make:

10
00:00:32,388 --> 00:00:34,526
a message on Comms from the Morrigan,

11
00:00:34,976 --> 00:00:37,035
with the objective's name as its title.

12
00:00:37,935 --> 00:00:39,632
Two lines in her file make it.

13
00:00:40,532 --> 00:00:42,555
Speaker says who gives the warning,

14
00:00:43,005 --> 00:00:47,042
and here it's a role: the name of her flagship, in small letters.

15
00:00:47,942 --> 00:00:50,364
Signal says is what she sends.

16
00:00:52,164 --> 00:00:55,607
Where I write the word time, in curly brackets,

17
00:00:56,057 --> 00:00:58,213
the game puts in the time that's left.

18
00:00:59,113 --> 00:01:03,858
It's sent at five minutes, at two, at one, and at thirty seconds,

19
00:01:04,308 --> 00:01:06,766
and only the ones that fit inside your limit.

20
00:01:07,966 --> 00:01:10,224
Now run lint, and it complains.

21
00:01:11,124 --> 00:01:13,896
It says morrigan isn't in the cast.

22
00:01:15,696 --> 00:01:17,515
And here, that warning is wrong.

23
00:01:18,415 --> 00:01:21,677
Lint's looking for a person, in a Characters section,

24
00:01:22,127 --> 00:01:23,498
and the Morrigan is a ship.

25
00:01:24,398 --> 00:01:26,307
The game looks for a character first,

26
00:01:26,757 --> 00:01:29,997
and then for a ship wearing that role, and it finds her.

27
00:01:30,897 --> 00:01:35,815
So this is the only warning in the whole course that I'll tell you to keep.

28
00:01:36,715 --> 00:01:37,956
Read it every time, though.

29
00:01:38,406 --> 00:01:41,856
If the name in it isn't on your Named line, then it's true.

30
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:45,871
For testing, I've set the limit to three minutes.

31
00:01:46,771 --> 00:01:48,702
She arrives, and I do nothing.

32
00:01:49,602 --> 00:01:52,478
About a minute later, Comms gets a message from the Morrigan,

33
00:01:52,928 --> 00:01:54,986
with the objective's name as its title.

34
00:01:56,786 --> 00:01:58,321
You have two minutes, little ship.

35
00:01:58,771 --> 00:02:00,645
Then this sector is mine.

36
00:02:01,545 --> 00:02:03,336
That's her voice, in my words,

37
00:02:03,786 --> 00:02:05,744
and it's in the one file.

38
00:02:06,644 --> 00:02:09,428
If I send that file to a friend, they hear it too.

39
00:02:10,628 --> 00:02:12,058
Now for the call itself.

40
00:02:12,958 --> 00:02:15,123
On Comms it waits in Incoming Hails,

41
00:02:15,573 --> 00:02:17,817
under her name and the title I give it.

42
00:02:18,717 --> 00:02:21,323
You know the three parts from your own mission:

43
00:02:21,773 --> 00:02:25,169
a Beat that places it, a cast, and a scene.

44
00:02:26,069 --> 00:02:27,630
All three go in the boss file,

45
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:30,033
and I start with the Beat.

46
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:36,049
It has an Action line that says, queen hails, and a scene's key.

47
00:02:36,949 --> 00:02:39,302
I run lint, and there's a second warning,

48
00:02:39,752 --> 00:02:41,166
and this one is true.

49
00:02:42,066 --> 00:02:44,490
The Beat names a scene that nobody has written yet,

50
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:47,359
so right now, no call would come.

51
00:02:48,559 --> 00:02:50,410
Here's the call opened on Comms:

52
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:53,934
her face, her name, her offer, and an answer.

53
00:02:54,834 --> 00:02:57,534
To make it, I go to the very end of the file,

54
00:02:57,984 --> 00:03:00,599
and I type two sections you already know.

55
00:03:01,499 --> 00:03:04,438
Characters, with the Queen and her first mate.

56
00:03:05,338 --> 00:03:07,900
And Dialogue, with one scene.

57
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:12,674
The sections have two hashes, like her objectives,

58
00:03:13,124 --> 00:03:16,325
and the people and the scenes inside them have three.

59
00:03:17,225 --> 00:03:19,984
The scene is just what you wrote in Lecture 3:

60
00:03:20,434 --> 00:03:23,348
a speaker, two blocks of takes, and an answer.

61
00:03:24,248 --> 00:03:26,205
That answer finishes the Beat.

62
00:03:28,005 --> 00:03:31,561
I run lint again, and the warning about the call has gone.

63
00:03:32,761 --> 00:03:34,282
There's nothing to paste for this.

64
00:03:35,181 --> 00:03:38,721
When she arrives, the Siege reads her file itself.

65
00:03:39,621 --> 00:03:41,749
Her objectives go to the crew,

66
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:43,885
her people come into the game,

67
00:03:44,335 --> 00:03:46,786
and her scenes are made ready to be called.

68
00:03:48,586 --> 00:03:50,368
Two things follow from that.

69
00:03:51,268 --> 00:03:53,606
Her people don't exist until she arrives,

70
00:03:54,056 --> 00:03:57,154
which is fine, because her Beats don't either.

71
00:03:58,054 --> 00:03:59,934
And her card isn't part of this at all.

72
00:04:00,834 --> 00:04:02,595
It still brings the third ship,

73
00:04:03,045 --> 00:04:04,781
and I haven't added a line to it.

74
00:04:05,981 --> 00:04:07,264
Now I make an answer matter.

75
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:10,009
Here's where it ends up on Comms:

76
00:04:10,459 --> 00:04:13,666
First Mate Orla on the line, with two answers of her own.

77
00:04:14,566 --> 00:04:17,205
A second answer leads to a second scene,

78
00:04:17,655 --> 00:04:20,229
where the Badb's first mate comes on the line.

79
00:04:21,129 --> 00:04:23,584
And if the crew says, then fly with us,

80
00:04:24,034 --> 00:04:26,091
three things happen after the semicolon.

81
00:04:27,891 --> 00:04:29,861
First, the call is finished.

82
00:04:30,761 --> 00:04:35,381
Turn the Badb is finished, which reveals one more step.

83
00:04:36,281 --> 00:04:38,337
And that step has an Action of its own:

84
00:04:38,787 --> 00:04:40,320
badb joins T S N.

85
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,841
So the ship changes sides.

86
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:46,407
In the Quest Log, on Helm's handheld,

87
00:04:46,857 --> 00:04:50,357
The Badb Turns appears, with her ship drawn at the top.

88
00:04:52,157 --> 00:04:54,694
Notice where I typed those two records:

89
00:04:55,144 --> 00:04:58,143
among her objectives, above the Characters line.

90
00:04:59,044 --> 00:05:02,138
Her people and her scenes stay last in the file.

91
00:05:03,338 --> 00:05:04,907
Check both, and then play it.

92
00:05:05,807 --> 00:05:10,171
On Comms, there's her call, waiting in Incoming Hails,

93
00:05:10,621 --> 00:05:12,337
with her name and the title.

94
00:05:13,237 --> 00:05:14,955
I open it, she makes her offer,

95
00:05:15,405 --> 00:05:17,307
and I talk to the Badb instead.

96
00:05:19,107 --> 00:05:21,311
I choose, then fly with us.

97
00:05:22,211 --> 00:05:24,492
Helm shows it one line at a time,

98
00:05:24,942 --> 00:05:27,727
and the last line says, the Badb turns.

99
00:05:28,627 --> 00:05:33,534
In the Quest Log, the call is done, the Badb has turned,

100
00:05:33,984 --> 00:05:36,794
and the bonus for sinking her has failed.

101
00:05:37,694 --> 00:05:39,322
That's a real choice for the crew:

102
00:05:39,772 --> 00:05:42,513
three hundred credits, or one raider fewer.

103
00:05:43,413 --> 00:05:45,401
Then play it again and refuse her,

104
00:05:45,851 --> 00:05:48,897
and play it a third time and never answer at all.

105
00:05:49,797 --> 00:05:52,275
The game has to be winnable on every road.

106
00:05:53,475 --> 00:05:54,983
Now, what are you handing over?

107
00:05:55,883 --> 00:05:58,355
Nearly all of her is the one file.

108
00:05:59,255 --> 00:06:00,758
Send just that one file,

109
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:04,567
and your friend gets the boss, her ships, her objectives,

110
00:06:05,017 --> 00:06:06,532
the Morrigan calling the clock,

111
00:06:06,982 --> 00:06:10,581
and the Queen's call with the answer that turns the Badb.

112
00:06:12,381 --> 00:06:15,752
What they don't get is the arrival line and the reserve ship.

113
00:06:16,652 --> 00:06:18,536
Those two are her card,

114
00:06:18,986 --> 00:06:22,585
and the card lives in a folder inside Legendary Missions.

115
00:06:23,485 --> 00:06:26,756
An update removes that folder, for them and for you.

116
00:06:27,656 --> 00:06:29,734
So keep a copy outside the game.

117
00:06:30,634 --> 00:06:34,124
Lint will tell you: one warning when the folder's there,

118
00:06:34,574 --> 00:06:36,012
and two when it isn't.

119
00:06:37,212 --> 00:06:38,737
The page ends with a rubric,

120
00:06:39,188 --> 00:06:42,446
and every line on it is something you can check yourself.

121
00:06:43,346 --> 00:06:47,563
She's yours, she's checked, she plays, and she travels.

122
00:06:49,363 --> 00:06:52,223
When every line is ticked, you've finished Class 2.

123
00:06:53,123 --> 00:06:55,637
You can write a cast, a conversation,

124
00:06:56,087 --> 00:06:57,810
and a boss who talks back.

125
00:06:58,710 --> 00:07:01,213
In the next class, the crew leaves the bridge.
